{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam configuration and documentation","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG",".bridge_state/projects.json","status","type","link","priority","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","migration","provider-neutral","mapping seam","backward compatibility","reuse contract"],"propositions":["The mapping seam configuration surface and behaviors require end-to-end documentation across config reference, provider-neutral design guide, and migration notes.","The feature must be portable across diverse CI environments with injected-transport unit tests and no live Jira or CI-specific dependencies required.","Migration and rollback must be safe: absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior exactly, with deletion as the rollback path.","The provider-neutral core must be documented as the reuse seam for future integrations (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) while deferring direct support to out-of-scope work."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787874457524597001,"uuid":"4fa7309c-e1e6-49db-908e-8da4d7a26c44"}